WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:37.489
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:37.759 --> 00:38.280
Oh, man!

3
00:38.560 --> 00:39.320
Star reporter Shen!

4
00:39.880 --> 00:40.560
Hello, hello, hello!

5
00:41.560 --> 00:42.640
I'm Factory Director Ma Guowen.

6
00:43.119 --> 00:43.719
Hello, Director Ma.

7
00:44.439 --> 00:44.880
Sorry to keep you waiting.

8
00:44.960 --> 00:45.840
I'll show you around first,

9
00:45.840 --> 00:46.679
then you can interview me.

10
00:46.799 --> 00:47.200
Let's go, let's go.

11
00:47.200 --> 00:47.560
Come on.

12
00:50.840 --> 00:51.840
That's the workshop over there,

13
00:52.200 --> 00:53.280
and that's my office.

14
00:53.359 --> 00:54.119
After that, you can interview me.

15
00:54.320 --> 00:55.280
Zhao Haipeng!

16
00:55.719 --> 00:57.320
It's Zhao Haipeng from Publicity.

17
00:57.920 --> 00:59.520
Come to the Area One workshop.

18
00:59.560 --> 01:00.520
Hurry up!

19
01:01.520 --> 01:02.399
Zhao Haipeng!

20
01:02.399 --> 01:03.439
Rushing me like crazy... Publicity...

21
01:03.439 --> 01:04.159
Seriously... Zhao Haipeng!

22
01:04.359 --> 01:06.400
Come to the Bottling Workshop in Area One.

23
01:06.400 --> 01:07.400
Hurry up!

24
01:11.719 --> 01:12.319
Comrade Reporter!

25
01:12.640 --> 01:13.079
Hello!

26
01:13.480 --> 01:14.760
I'm Zhao Haipeng from Publicity.

27
01:16.280 --> 01:16.840
Hello.

28
01:16.959 --> 01:18.200
Shen Leshui from Lacheng TV.

29
01:19.239 --> 01:20.239
My chain slipped off earlier.

30
01:22.439 --> 01:23.159
I mean...

31
01:23.239 --> 01:23.719
you know...

32
01:23.879 --> 01:25.159
My bike... bike chain slipped off.

33
01:26.519 --> 01:27.159
What was your name again?

34
01:28.040 --> 01:28.640
Shen Leshui.

35
01:29.439 --> 01:30.519
Our Lapi Brewery,

36
01:30.599 --> 01:32.319
riding the wave of reform,

37
01:32.519 --> 01:34.200
is full of drive right now!

38
01:34.239 --> 01:35.680
Production has really ramped up.

39
01:36.359 --> 01:36.920
In a little while,

40
01:37.040 --> 01:38.480
we'll all gather by the entrance,

41
01:38.519 --> 01:40.120
and take a lively group photo.

42
01:40.200 --> 01:40.959
A big group photo!

43
01:41.159 --> 01:42.640
Show off our brand-new look!

44
01:43.159 --> 01:45.719
This is Cheng Youtian from Bottling.

45
01:46.280 --> 01:47.319
He does great work! "I love Lapi!"

46
01:48.120 --> 01:48.799
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

47
01:48.920 --> 01:49.959
Group photo, group photo!

48
01:50.799 --> 01:51.159
Quick, quick, quick!

49
01:51.159 --> 01:51.560
Well...

50
01:52.000 --> 01:53.680
Right, our second-in-command is right!

51
01:54.359 --> 01:56.400
Let's all take a big group photo!

52
01:57.239 --> 01:58.959
Today we take the 20th century's...

53
01:59.079 --> 02:01.640
most important group photo for Lapi Brewery!

54
02:01.719 --> 02:03.079
Everyone, look happy!

55
02:03.079 --> 02:03.959
Great!

56
02:05.400 --> 02:06.400
Hey, Reporter...

57
02:06.799 --> 02:07.239
Right, right.

58
02:07.560 --> 02:07.959
Reporter!

59
02:08.039 --> 02:09.280
Get in the photo with us!

60
02:09.479 --> 02:10.120
We can't do it without you!

61
02:10.120 --> 02:10.639
Come on, come on.

62
02:11.560 --> 02:12.120
Come over here.

63
02:12.120 --> 02:12.840
Join in, join in!

64
02:12.960 --> 02:13.800
Stand in the middle.

65
02:14.439 --> 02:15.639
All right, follow my lead!

66
02:16.120 --> 02:17.159
"Lapi is my home!"

67
02:17.479 --> 02:18.960
Ready, go!

68
02:19.159 --> 02:21.439
Lapi is my home,

69
02:21.680 --> 02:24.400
and we all love it!

70
02:24.680 --> 02:26.159
Yeah!

71
04:03.039 --> 04:03.639
How much do you weigh?

72
04:03.639 --> 04:04.719
About 120 to 130 jin.

73
04:05.319 --> 04:06.400
How much did Ma Guowen weigh?

74
04:06.520 --> 04:07.960
About the same as me.

75
04:08.639 --> 04:10.240
Dead weight is heavier than living weight.

76
04:10.960 --> 04:11.919
Don't walk.

77
04:12.199 --> 04:12.719
I won't.

78
04:12.719 --> 04:13.680
Walking ruins the reenactment.

79
04:13.960 --> 04:14.800
Do you have any strength left?

80
04:14.800 --> 04:15.120
Yeah.

81
04:15.719 --> 04:17.759
From the factory office to here,

82
04:18.319 --> 04:19.199
how long did it take?

83
04:19.399 --> 04:20.360
Less than 20 minutes.

84
04:20.759 --> 04:21.600
Let's stop here for now, bro.

85
04:25.199 --> 04:26.040
I can't carry you anymore.

86
04:26.839 --> 04:28.000
This guy's got incredible stamina.

87
04:28.759 --> 04:29.759
Then why did he

88
04:30.439 --> 04:31.399
spend all that time

89
04:31.399 --> 04:33.120
dragging him from the office to the tracks,

90
04:33.279 --> 04:34.959
and even posing him on his knees?

91
04:35.560 --> 04:36.279
What was he after?

92
04:36.839 --> 04:38.959
Just so the train would smash him to pieces?

93
04:38.959 --> 04:39.480
Or...

94
04:40.240 --> 04:41.639
did he have another motive?

95
04:42.560 --> 04:43.519
To confuse the investigation.

96
04:47.160 --> 04:48.680
It snowed so heavily last night,

97
04:49.560 --> 04:50.480
and the wind was blowing hard.

98
04:52.160 --> 04:53.439
Nobody comes out here.

99
04:54.519 --> 04:55.560
No eyewitnesses,

100
04:56.360 --> 04:57.560
no surveillance cameras,

101
05:00.720 --> 05:02.360
and the snow covered all the footprints.

102
05:02.959 --> 05:03.639
No cameras,

103
05:03.639 --> 05:04.800
no witnesses,

104
05:04.800 --> 05:06.920
not even any footprints.

105
05:06.920 --> 05:08.560
So we basically have no clues at all.

106
05:15.279 --> 05:16.600
The victim, Ma Guowen,

107
05:16.879 --> 05:18.240
was 58 years old,

108
05:18.680 --> 05:19.759
174 centimeters tall,

109
05:20.199 --> 05:21.560
and weighed 62 kilograms.

110
05:22.199 --> 05:24.360
Comminuted fracture on the left skull.

111
05:24.439 --> 05:26.439
Congestion in both eyelids and conjunctiva.

112
05:26.959 --> 05:28.319
Edema at the margins of the conjunctiva.

113
05:28.959 --> 05:30.160
The cause of death was determined

114
05:30.399 --> 05:32.079
to be craniocerebral injury.

115
05:33.319 --> 05:34.800
The plastic bag over the victim's head

116
05:35.000 --> 05:36.639
shows no signs of stretching or deformation.

117
05:36.920 --> 05:38.120
Only biological traces

118
05:38.120 --> 05:39.439
belonging to Ma Guowen were found on it.

119
05:40.199 --> 05:41.160
None from anyone else.

120
05:42.240 --> 05:43.560
The crime scene was also cleaned up.

121
05:44.519 --> 05:45.079
Furthermore,

122
05:45.079 --> 05:46.680
the killer was swift,

123
05:46.959 --> 05:47.600
very strong,

124
05:47.600 --> 05:50.399
and had counter-investigation skills.

125
05:51.000 --> 05:53.120
Given what we know about the factory,

126
05:53.600 --> 05:55.639
the killer had plenty of time to strike.

127
05:56.120 --> 05:58.800
According to the autopsy report,

128
05:58.959 --> 05:59.920
the victim had likely eaten

129
05:59.920 --> 06:01.839
a heavy dinner shortly before he died.

130
06:02.240 --> 06:04.680
Plus, there were no signs of a struggle.

131
06:06.000 --> 06:06.959
That indicates

132
06:07.079 --> 06:08.319
it was someone he knew.

133
06:10.199 --> 06:12.399
Tell us about Ma Guowen's social connections.

134
06:13.399 --> 06:13.839
Right.

135
06:15.319 --> 06:15.959
Well,

136
06:16.120 --> 06:17.160
Lapi Brewery

137
06:17.439 --> 06:19.199
used to be the local economic pillar.

138
06:19.439 --> 06:20.680
Back when I was in school,

139
06:20.839 --> 06:22.120
anyone working there

140
06:22.360 --> 06:23.519
was a big deal.

141
06:23.879 --> 06:25.959
So Director Ma's connections

142
06:26.120 --> 06:27.480
must be quite extensive.

143
06:28.680 --> 06:30.560
Based on what you just said,

144
06:30.800 --> 06:33.600
and what came out

145
06:34.439 --> 06:35.360
in Ma Guowen's autopsy report,

146
06:35.600 --> 06:36.879
I've summed up a few key points.

147
06:37.560 --> 06:38.040
One:

148
06:39.120 --> 06:40.040
it's someone he knew.

149
06:41.800 --> 06:42.560
Two:

150
06:42.800 --> 06:43.519
they must be physically strong.

151
06:44.199 --> 06:45.560
Three: they have a grudge.

152
06:45.839 --> 06:48.240
Four: they have counter-investigation skills.

153
06:48.480 --> 06:49.240
Someone he knew...

154
06:49.720 --> 06:50.439
Who could that be?

155
06:52.040 --> 06:53.240
Factory veterans?

156
06:53.639 --> 06:55.759
But there's one problem with old-timers:

157
06:55.959 --> 06:57.360
would they have the strength

158
06:57.759 --> 06:59.079
to haul Ma Guowen around?

159
06:59.360 --> 07:00.959
If they're in good shape,

160
07:01.160 --> 07:02.560
they could be street thugs.

161
07:04.000 --> 07:04.959
Is that a possibility?

162
07:06.360 --> 07:07.120
Street thugs

163
07:07.480 --> 07:08.920
holding a grudge against Ma Guowen.

164
07:09.399 --> 07:10.959
Since Ma Guowen was selling the factory,

165
07:11.439 --> 07:13.680
disputes could have flared up.

166
07:14.399 --> 07:15.279
Then again, there's another issue.

167
07:15.279 --> 07:16.199
If they're street thugs,

168
07:16.360 --> 07:18.160
would they have counter-investigation skills?

169
07:18.360 --> 07:18.720
Right.

170
07:18.720 --> 07:20.399
Some street thugs are good at evading police,

171
07:20.519 --> 07:22.160
but from our investigation,

172
07:22.439 --> 07:25.839
this person knows the brewery inside out.

173
07:26.279 --> 07:27.240
So would street thugs

174
07:27.600 --> 07:28.839
really know the brewery that well,

175
07:29.240 --> 07:30.800
and have those counter-investigation skills?

176
07:31.560 --> 07:33.040
Based on the points I just went through,

177
07:34.360 --> 07:36.720
I've narrowed down the suspect profile.

178
07:37.240 --> 07:37.920
Let's

179
07:38.000 --> 07:40.040
focus our search within this scope:

180
07:40.720 --> 07:42.120
a physically strong male,

181
07:42.639 --> 07:44.959
connected to Ma Guowen or Lapi Brewery,

182
07:45.399 --> 07:46.519
holding a grudge.

183
07:47.079 --> 07:48.319
On top of that, the suspect

184
07:48.360 --> 07:49.240
has to be sharp,

185
07:50.279 --> 07:51.480
and skilled in counter-investigation.

186
07:52.000 --> 07:52.759
What do you think?

187
08:02.360 --> 08:03.480
Are bottle caps really that fun?

188
08:07.120 --> 08:08.079
Are you even listening to me?

189
08:08.800 --> 08:09.759
I'm listening, bro.

190
08:10.759 --> 08:11.759
You got a different opinion?

191
08:12.720 --> 08:13.120
No.

192
08:13.120 --> 08:14.680
I think your analysis is spot on.

193
08:16.079 --> 08:18.040
Just one little question, though.

194
08:18.199 --> 08:20.920
I might've lost track earlier.

195
08:21.199 --> 08:23.720
How did we deduce that the suspect

196
08:23.720 --> 08:26.399
is likely a strong, able-bodied man

197
08:26.399 --> 08:27.279
with great stamina?

198
08:28.399 --> 08:29.680
Carrying you on my back,

199
08:30.079 --> 08:32.039
I hadn't even reached the tracks from the office,

200
08:32.039 --> 08:32.960
just reaching the old smokestack,

201
08:32.960 --> 08:33.679
I was already completely exhausted.

202
08:33.679 --> 08:34.519
It took 20 minutes.

203
08:34.639 --> 08:36.200
How could this person not have crazy stamina?

204
08:36.480 --> 08:38.120
Didn't we also mention back then

205
08:38.120 --> 08:40.200
that they might've used tools?

206
08:40.480 --> 08:41.720
A handcart, a flatbed cart,

207
08:41.960 --> 08:43.200
or even a car are all possible.

208
08:43.480 --> 08:45.000
The snow covered everything anyway,

209
08:45.120 --> 08:46.320
so we couldn't see tire tracks anyway.

210
08:48.480 --> 08:49.200
Fine, sure.

211
08:49.600 --> 08:51.000
Then you go find that handcart,

212
08:51.120 --> 08:52.320
flatbed cart, or car.

213
08:52.879 --> 08:53.600
Track it down.

214
08:54.039 --> 08:54.759
Anything's possible,

215
08:54.799 --> 08:55.320
right?

216
08:57.200 --> 08:57.679
Right.

217
08:57.919 --> 09:00.399
Well, the new info I have is...

218
09:00.399 --> 09:01.759
I think his MO

219
09:01.799 --> 09:02.679
is really quite unique.

220
09:02.759 --> 09:04.120
First of all, we all know

221
09:04.159 --> 09:06.399
his MO is very ritualistic.

222
09:06.679 --> 09:08.039
A bottle cap was embedded in the head.

223
09:08.759 --> 09:09.600
This bottle cap...

224
09:09.600 --> 09:10.879
Wait, aren't we discussing

225
09:10.960 --> 09:12.240
the murder weapons?

226
09:13.279 --> 09:14.519
Why are we talking about the bottle cap again?

227
09:14.960 --> 09:17.159
And I already had Wenxiu look into the bottle cap.

228
09:18.600 --> 09:18.960
Right.

229
09:19.320 --> 09:20.679
She turned up some info.

230
09:21.120 --> 09:22.840
Back in 1999,

231
09:23.159 --> 09:24.320
the brewery...

232
09:24.399 --> 09:27.039
to celebrate the millennium,

233
09:28.080 --> 09:28.799
made this.

234
09:28.799 --> 09:30.320
To celebrate the coming of the new millennium,

235
09:30.360 --> 09:32.039
they put out a special commemorative edition.

236
09:32.240 --> 09:34.279
And back then, they solicited

237
09:34.360 --> 09:36.559
public design submissions.

238
09:36.679 --> 09:38.159
This design was chosen in the end.

239
09:38.399 --> 09:39.399
This design

240
09:40.039 --> 09:41.480
was only in circulation for one year.

241
09:41.480 --> 09:43.279
Meaning the cap on the victim's head

242
09:43.279 --> 09:44.720
has long been out of production.

243
09:45.120 --> 09:46.240
They don't exist anymore.

244
09:47.720 --> 09:48.440
Back in 1999,

245
09:48.440 --> 09:50.000
wasn't there someone named Liu Xuemei,

246
09:50.000 --> 09:50.799
a female beer taster,

247
09:50.879 --> 09:52.039
who accidentally froze to death?

248
09:52.200 --> 09:53.519
Froze to death accidentally after drinking?

249
09:54.000 --> 09:55.440
That was so many years ago.

250
09:55.679 --> 09:56.879
Besides, it wasn't even a case.

251
09:57.120 --> 09:58.200
Because a case was never opened.

252
09:58.519 --> 09:59.519
Something from over a decade ago,

253
09:59.519 --> 10:01.600
what does it have to do with Ma Guowen's case today?

254
10:01.799 --> 10:02.600
It's connected.

255
10:02.960 --> 10:03.399
Bro,

256
10:03.840 --> 10:05.240
the connection between them is

257
10:05.559 --> 10:08.759
at the scene where Liu Xuemei froze to death,

258
10:08.960 --> 10:11.360
there was also a bottle cap just like this.

259
10:11.879 --> 10:12.759
How do you know that?

260
10:12.919 --> 10:14.080
It was all over the news.

261
10:17.000 --> 10:17.960
How old were you in '99?

262
10:20.000 --> 10:20.879
Seven or eight.

263
10:22.240 --> 10:23.200
A seven- or eight-year-old kid...

264
10:23.240 --> 10:24.240
didn't watch cartoons,

265
10:24.600 --> 10:25.480
but watched the news?

266
10:27.080 --> 10:28.759
Is that what a kid that age does?

267
10:28.759 --> 10:29.080
No...

268
10:29.120 --> 10:30.840
I watched cartoons back then, too.

269
10:30.840 --> 10:31.200
Wait, no.

270
10:31.200 --> 10:33.399
I didn't watch that news when I was a kid.

271
10:33.440 --> 10:34.320
Then when did you watch it?

272
10:34.320 --> 10:36.360
I watched it seven or eight hours ago.

273
10:36.519 --> 10:38.240
Seven or eight hours ago,

274
10:38.240 --> 10:40.240
you watched news from over a decade ago?

275
10:40.440 --> 10:41.639
Shen Leshui told me to watch it.

276
10:41.960 --> 10:43.799
She said she represented the TV station back then

277
10:43.919 --> 10:44.679
to cover Liu Xuemei's death.

278
10:44.679 --> 10:45.639
Wait, Shen Leshui?

279
10:45.639 --> 10:47.000
When did she tell you to watch the news?

280
10:47.000 --> 10:47.759
How come I didn't know?

281
10:48.519 --> 10:50.279
She told me when we questioned her that day.

282
10:51.159 --> 10:52.000
I was there when we questioned her.

283
10:52.000 --> 10:52.879
I didn't hear that.

284
10:53.159 --> 10:53.840
She said it.

285
10:54.320 --> 10:55.279
She didn't.

286
10:55.320 --> 10:55.960
She did.

287
10:56.080 --> 10:57.279
You stepped out for a second.

288
10:57.440 --> 10:58.519
Just in that brief moment,

289
10:58.679 --> 10:59.559
she told me.

290
11:01.600 --> 11:02.799
In that split second I was out,

291
11:03.600 --> 11:04.720
you two sure talked a lot.

292
11:11.200 --> 11:11.879
Shen Leshui.

293
11:13.919 --> 11:15.159
Okay, I'll head over right now.

294
11:18.200 --> 11:18.879
Shen Leshui

295
11:19.919 --> 11:21.080
says she received a threatening letter.

296
11:35.759 --> 11:37.840
Lapi Brewery used to be a state-owned plant.

297
11:38.320 --> 11:39.399
After it was restructured,

298
11:39.399 --> 11:41.240
Director Ma Guowen bought it at auction

299
11:41.679 --> 11:42.759
and made it his own.

300
11:43.080 --> 11:44.320
Over the years,

301
11:44.399 --> 11:45.679
many workers left,

302
11:45.679 --> 11:46.759
and it shrank in size.

303
11:46.799 --> 11:47.600
Now he wanted to flip it.

304
11:48.519 --> 11:49.480
Did the killer murder him

305
11:49.480 --> 11:50.559
to stop him from selling the plant?

306
11:53.279 --> 11:54.279
Stop him from selling?

307
11:55.200 --> 11:56.639
Then why go through the trouble

308
11:56.679 --> 11:58.960
of moving the body to the old tracks?

309
12:00.879 --> 12:01.840
To make a scene, of course.

310
12:03.360 --> 12:04.440
The bigger the fuss, the better.

311
12:04.639 --> 12:05.559
So no one would buy it.

312
12:06.200 --> 12:07.200
Does that make sense?

313
12:08.519 --> 12:09.919
Hardly anyone visits the old plant.

314
12:10.759 --> 12:11.679
Leaving it at the new plant

315
12:11.720 --> 12:12.440
would cause a bigger stir.

316
12:16.879 --> 12:18.039
Then that means he

317
12:19.360 --> 12:20.960
knew someone would be filming that day,

318
12:21.559 --> 12:22.879
and deliberately put the body there.

319
12:24.440 --> 12:25.759
So does this killer

320
12:25.919 --> 12:27.000
have any connection

321
12:27.879 --> 12:29.320
to the person filming?

322
12:30.080 --> 12:31.080
Wasn't the person filming...

323
12:32.039 --> 12:33.039
Shen Leshui?

324
12:34.039 --> 12:35.720
He wanted Shen Leshui

325
12:35.759 --> 12:37.039
to film Ma Guowen's dead body.

326
12:38.440 --> 12:39.120
Bro, if you put it that way,

327
12:39.120 --> 12:40.080
that's terrifying.

328
12:41.279 --> 12:42.679
Shen Leshui has been away for how many years?

329
12:43.080 --> 12:43.919
Over a decade.

330
12:44.080 --> 12:44.720
And right as she returns,

331
12:44.720 --> 12:45.480
Ma Guowen ends up dead.

332
12:50.519 --> 12:52.600
Besides, Ma Guowen asked her to film, right?

333
12:55.320 --> 12:56.639
Now she's received a threat letter.

334
12:58.159 --> 12:59.039
Let's go ask her.

335
13:18.279 --> 13:19.039
Who is it?

336
13:30.480 --> 13:31.200
Leshui.

337
13:32.000 --> 13:32.960
Are you all right?

338
13:34.600 --> 13:35.120
Just shaken up.

339
13:36.960 --> 13:38.000
Is anything missing from your home?

340
13:38.159 --> 13:39.039
No, nothing like that.

341
13:39.279 --> 13:40.240
Where's the threatening letter?

342
13:47.519 --> 13:49.279
"Don't come looking to die here.

343
13:50.440 --> 13:50.960
Get lost."

344
13:54.919 --> 13:55.559
Don't be scared.

345
13:56.320 --> 13:56.919
By the way...

346
13:56.960 --> 13:58.440
Who lives across the hall?

347
13:59.159 --> 13:59.720
Tu Chunyan.

348
14:00.159 --> 14:01.519
A laid-off worker from Lapi Brewery.

349
14:01.960 --> 14:02.679
Last night,

350
14:02.679 --> 14:04.080
a man named Qian Yichuan came to see her.

351
14:04.200 --> 14:05.000
Qian Yichuan?

352
14:05.240 --> 14:06.840
The guard from Lapi Brewery?

353
14:07.039 --> 14:08.159
The one who walks with a limp?

354
14:08.600 --> 14:09.720
I don't know what he does,

355
14:09.720 --> 14:10.840
but he was here last night.

356
14:12.639 --> 14:14.080
Tu Chunyan kept dumping trash outside,

357
14:14.240 --> 14:15.159
so I reported her to property management.

358
14:15.159 --> 14:15.799
She was furious,

359
14:16.519 --> 14:17.720
but she wouldn't do something like this.

360
14:17.840 --> 14:19.320
Living this close would make it too obvious.

361
14:19.679 --> 14:20.960
Let me ask you something.

362
14:21.639 --> 14:23.519
Why did Ma Guowen always hire you to film?

363
14:24.279 --> 14:25.600
Back in 2000, it was you.

364
14:25.919 --> 14:27.080
Then over ten years passed,

365
14:27.080 --> 14:28.200
and the moment you returned, he hired you again.

366
14:28.600 --> 14:30.440
Do you two have some special connection?

367
14:30.960 --> 14:33.000
Also, he gave you 30,000 yuan.

368
14:33.279 --> 14:35.360
Did you write an IOU or sign a receipt?

369
14:35.600 --> 14:36.519
You shouldn't be asking me that.

370
14:36.519 --> 14:37.440
You should ask him.

371
14:37.600 --> 14:38.840
Isn't he dead?

372
14:39.080 --> 14:41.080
Only you know why he kept reaching out to you.

373
14:41.799 --> 14:43.559
First of all, he didn't keep reaching out to me.

374
14:44.080 --> 14:44.759
Over ten years ago,

375
14:44.759 --> 14:46.279
it was an assignment from Lacheng TV.

376
14:46.279 --> 14:47.399
I barely knew him.

377
14:47.480 --> 14:49.360
This time, we bumped into each other on the street.

378
14:52.120 --> 14:52.759
Bumped into each other?

379
14:54.039 --> 14:54.840
What a coincidence.

380
15:01.039 --> 15:01.519
Leshui.

381
15:02.840 --> 15:04.720
Did Ma Guowen ever mention

382
15:04.720 --> 15:06.120
wanting aerial shots,

383
15:06.200 --> 15:08.440
or filming the railroad tracks?

384
15:09.200 --> 15:10.320
He never mentioned the tracks.

385
15:11.120 --> 15:12.600
Aerial shots made him really excited, though.

386
15:13.000 --> 15:14.039
He insisted on getting aerial footage.

387
15:14.240 --> 15:15.759
And then you happened to capture it.

388
15:15.799 --> 15:16.519
Officer Han,

389
15:16.840 --> 15:18.480
do you also think Ma Guowen's death

390
15:18.480 --> 15:19.399
has something to do with me?

391
15:19.639 --> 15:21.440
Or that I shouldn't be seeking protection,

392
15:21.519 --> 15:22.559
but should be suspected instead?

393
15:22.960 --> 15:23.639
No.

394
15:23.840 --> 15:24.480
Never suspected you.

395
15:24.639 --> 15:26.200
Your ex-husband Zhao Haipeng,

396
15:26.240 --> 15:27.519
the gatekeeper Qian Yichuan,

397
15:27.519 --> 15:29.440
and the forklift driver Cao Jun—

398
15:29.600 --> 15:31.279
after the factory was restructured,

399
15:31.320 --> 15:32.320
they all stepped down as old workers.

400
15:32.440 --> 15:34.120
They probably didn't get along with Ma Guowen.

401
15:35.000 --> 15:36.559
Haven't you caught up with them since you returned?

402
15:37.519 --> 15:40.320
You know these old Lapi Brewery workers quite well.

403
15:40.679 --> 15:41.639
Do you have relatives here?

404
15:46.120 --> 15:46.919
Just doing my job.

405
15:51.279 --> 15:52.120
Look at this.

406
15:52.440 --> 15:53.799
"Get out of Lapi Brewery Compound."

407
15:54.120 --> 15:56.120
Who do you think wants you to leave?

408
15:57.039 --> 15:57.559
Could it be that back then,

409
15:57.559 --> 15:59.240
you offended someone while shooting the documentary?

410
15:59.440 --> 16:00.519
How would I know?

411
16:01.320 --> 16:01.799
By the way,

412
16:02.279 --> 16:04.279
in the footage I shot,

413
16:04.279 --> 16:05.600
did you find any clues?

414
16:05.879 --> 16:07.360
Did the suspect leave any traces?

415
16:07.840 --> 16:08.919
I can't disclose that right now.

416
16:11.799 --> 16:13.240
I just want to know a bit more

417
16:13.240 --> 16:15.039
about the progress of Ma Guowen's case,

418
16:15.039 --> 16:16.879
out of concern for my own safety.

419
16:17.000 --> 16:17.399
Understood.

420
16:17.399 --> 16:17.879
After all...

421
16:23.200 --> 16:24.240
These are my personal belongings.

422
16:26.120 --> 16:26.759
Sorry about that.

423
16:27.240 --> 16:29.240
Lately, whenever I see black trash bags,

424
16:29.240 --> 16:30.120
I get a bit on edge.

425
16:30.720 --> 16:31.360
What's in here?

426
16:31.360 --> 16:32.159
Can I take a look?

427
16:33.279 --> 16:33.919
Raw footage tapes.

428
16:35.200 --> 16:36.080
May I take a look?

429
16:43.879 --> 16:45.159
Such precious raw footage,

430
16:45.159 --> 16:46.320
and you usually keep it in

431
16:46.320 --> 16:47.240
a black garbage bag like this?

432
16:47.480 --> 16:48.120
Yeah, I do.

433
16:48.320 --> 16:49.279
I've always kept it in here.

434
16:51.519 --> 16:52.360
Real classy.

435
16:55.120 --> 16:56.960
Unused footage from "Malt Kingdom"...

436
16:58.480 --> 16:59.440
All of these?

437
17:00.200 --> 17:01.759
Then there must be plenty of footage of Ma Guowen

438
17:01.759 --> 17:03.840
and the others in here.

439
17:04.319 --> 17:05.599
And around Millennium Eve,

440
17:05.599 --> 17:06.759
you went to shoot footage too, right?

441
17:07.440 --> 17:09.000
Does this have anything to do with me being threatened?

442
17:09.519 --> 17:10.559
Of course it does.

443
17:11.240 --> 17:12.640
Look, both times you filmed,

444
17:13.079 --> 17:15.839
it was right when the factory was being sold,

445
17:16.559 --> 17:17.680
and people ended up dead both times.

446
17:18.359 --> 17:19.279
Quite a coincidence.

447
17:20.039 --> 17:20.519
Tell you what,

448
17:20.839 --> 17:21.720
this stuff...

449
17:22.119 --> 17:23.359
We'll take it back to examine first,

450
17:23.880 --> 17:24.880
to see if there are any leads.

451
17:25.680 --> 17:26.319
No way.

452
17:28.000 --> 17:28.640
The tape is damaged.

453
17:28.960 --> 17:29.759
It won't play.

454
17:30.880 --> 17:31.359
We can...

455
17:31.359 --> 17:33.240
get a professional technician to fix it for you.

456
17:33.759 --> 17:35.119
If it's ruined, you can't afford to pay me back.

457
17:35.160 --> 17:36.880
If it gets ruined, how much should we pay you?

458
17:36.920 --> 17:37.720
It's priceless.

459
17:45.079 --> 17:45.799
Xiao Gao,

460
17:48.319 --> 17:49.119
did you bring evidence bags?

461
17:52.960 --> 17:54.039
Take all those threatening letters.

462
17:55.160 --> 17:56.160
Just the threatening letters?

463
17:57.000 --> 17:57.880
Nothing else?

464
17:58.519 --> 17:59.400
How about I take you in too?

465
18:05.599 --> 18:06.359
Well...

466
18:07.799 --> 18:09.960
He just wants to understand the situation better.

467
18:11.279 --> 18:11.680
You know,

468
18:11.680 --> 18:12.519
asking in detail

469
18:12.559 --> 18:13.519
helps solve the case.

470
18:15.279 --> 18:15.759
Listen,

471
18:15.799 --> 18:17.160
keep your door locked at home,

472
18:17.640 --> 18:19.079
keep your phone charged,

473
18:19.440 --> 18:20.160
and if anything happens,

474
18:20.160 --> 18:21.720
just call me like you did today.

475
18:25.640 --> 18:26.480
Thanks for your cooperation.

476
18:30.319 --> 18:30.880
We're heading out.

477
18:41.599 --> 18:42.160
Xiao Gao,

478
18:43.960 --> 18:46.200
when you worked cases with Qiang in Qingzhou,

479
18:46.200 --> 18:47.079
were you like this too?

480
18:48.039 --> 18:49.160
Running your mouth non-stop?

481
18:49.720 --> 18:50.799
Before the boss could even finish,

482
18:50.960 --> 18:52.279
you jumped in and said it all.

483
18:54.440 --> 18:56.119
I didn't use to talk so much.

484
18:56.480 --> 18:57.480
Brother Qiang insisted I speak up.

485
18:57.480 --> 18:58.839
If... If I didn't, he'd kick me.

486
18:59.160 --> 19:00.000
He even kicked you?

487
19:00.920 --> 19:02.039
Wasn't that for my own good?

488
19:02.119 --> 19:03.599
Now I'm all trained up.

489
19:04.519 --> 19:05.720
Mind your approach a bit.

490
19:06.599 --> 19:07.440
She's a victim.

491
19:08.119 --> 19:09.920
You can't turn her place into an interrogation room.

492
19:12.400 --> 19:13.599
The questions I asked

493
19:13.640 --> 19:15.359
were all related to her case.

494
19:16.119 --> 19:17.480
Who sent the threatening letters,

495
19:17.720 --> 19:19.039
why they wanted her to leave here,

496
19:19.519 --> 19:20.960
and earlier downstairs,

497
19:21.000 --> 19:22.440
when we analyzed why Ma Guowen

498
19:22.680 --> 19:24.000
always picked her to film.

499
19:24.039 --> 19:25.240
She didn't give clear answers to any of it.

500
19:26.119 --> 19:27.240
And that raw footage tape.

501
19:27.920 --> 19:29.279
Did you see that earlier, bro?

502
19:29.440 --> 19:30.799
The second I touched it, she snatched it back.

503
19:31.119 --> 19:32.240
There's definitely information on it.

504
19:32.599 --> 19:33.839
Why was she afraid to let us see it?

505
19:34.519 --> 19:36.039
Still, you can't just snatch it from her.

506
19:39.319 --> 19:40.240
Either way, I'm sure

507
19:40.559 --> 19:41.720
there are clues we need in there.

508
19:42.359 --> 19:43.240
Next chance I get,

509
19:43.240 --> 19:44.079
I'm asking her for it again.

510
19:45.839 --> 19:47.519
Did you notice anything else?

511
19:49.640 --> 19:50.599
Your shoe covers.

512
19:52.160 --> 19:52.920
It's snowing.

513
19:53.079 --> 19:54.160
Watch out, it's slippery.

514
19:59.960 --> 20:01.000
Didn't you lock the car?

515
20:02.559 --> 20:03.960
It acts up in this cold.

516
20:34.200 --> 20:36.759
Did he mention anything about aerial shots,

517
20:36.839 --> 20:38.759
or filming the railroad tracks?

518
20:39.920 --> 20:40.920
He didn't mention the tracks.

519
20:41.759 --> 20:43.279
Aerial shots really got him excited, though.

520
20:43.279 --> 20:44.240
He insisted on getting aerial shots.

521
20:44.599 --> 20:46.160
And then you captured it.

522
20:46.480 --> 20:47.119
Officer Han,

523
20:47.640 --> 20:49.400
do you think Ma Guowen's death

524
20:49.400 --> 20:50.319
has something to do with me?

525
20:50.319 --> 20:51.960
Or that I shouldn't be seeking protection,

526
20:52.000 --> 20:53.039
but should be suspected instead?

527
20:53.599 --> 20:54.119
No.

528
20:54.480 --> 20:55.000
We don't suspect you.

529
20:55.000 --> 20:55.680
We're just...

530
21:19.680 --> 21:20.880
You're in the news business.

531
21:21.039 --> 21:21.599
Investigating someone...

532
21:21.599 --> 21:22.880
why are you asking me for help?

533
21:23.279 --> 21:24.359
I don't have those skills.

534
21:24.559 --> 21:25.759
How about I introduce you to someone?

535
21:29.400 --> 21:30.319
Is he reliable?

536
21:35.480 --> 21:36.759
Chen, long time no see.

537
21:37.960 --> 21:38.880
Long time no see.

538
21:39.799 --> 21:41.119
Why are you back so early today?

539
21:41.359 --> 21:43.200
Didn't you say the station had an event tonight?

540
21:43.960 --> 21:45.480
I came back early to see Xiaohu.

541
21:46.160 --> 21:46.880
I'll let you two talk.

542
21:50.279 --> 21:51.279
How thoughtful.

543
21:51.880 --> 21:52.960
Tonight's the station anniversary.

544
21:53.680 --> 21:55.200
Everyone from the news department will be there.

545
21:55.519 --> 21:57.160
There's a guy named Li Mingyang who's pretty reliable.

546
21:58.400 --> 21:59.000
All right.

547
21:59.839 --> 22:00.519
Let's do that, then.

548
22:15.759 --> 22:16.759
Brother Chuang, have you been waiting long?

549
22:18.000 --> 22:18.599
No worries, it's fine.

550
22:19.160 --> 22:19.799
Wanna ask you something.

551
22:20.119 --> 22:20.599
Go ahead.

552
22:21.359 --> 22:22.440
Do you know Ma...

553
22:27.160 --> 22:28.559
You're no good, and neither is your car.

554
22:30.319 --> 22:30.880
Brother Chuang.

555
22:31.119 --> 22:32.720
What were... What were you saying about Ma who?

556
22:34.240 --> 22:36.160
I wanted to ask about Ma Guowen.

557
22:36.720 --> 22:38.680
Do you know who he offended recently?

558
22:39.079 --> 22:39.880
Who he offended?

559
22:41.039 --> 22:41.839
No idea.

560
22:42.160 --> 22:42.599
Anyway,

561
22:42.920 --> 22:44.279
that Ma Guowen,

562
22:44.599 --> 22:46.279
don't let his smiling face fool you.

563
22:46.279 --> 22:47.400
He's actually ruthless.

564
22:47.880 --> 22:50.000
Did you forget what happened to Lao Qian's leg?

565
22:51.119 --> 22:51.519
Besides,

566
22:51.519 --> 22:52.559
he's greedy and lecherous.

567
22:53.559 --> 22:54.119
Ma Guowen...

568
22:55.200 --> 22:56.680
did he clash with anyone recently?

569
22:57.680 --> 22:58.279
Cao Jun, obviously.

570
23:03.000 --> 23:04.119
The night before last at 11:00 PM,

571
23:04.319 --> 23:05.160
what were you doing?

572
23:06.759 --> 23:07.720
Nothing.

573
23:08.200 --> 23:09.920
I usually don't go out after 11:00.

574
23:10.359 --> 23:11.200
I was at home.

575
23:11.880 --> 23:12.319
Right.

576
23:12.440 --> 23:13.079
At... at home.

577
23:13.880 --> 23:15.519
Can you describe what you were doing at home?

578
23:22.440 --> 23:23.119
Eating.

579
23:23.880 --> 23:25.160
Drinking, watching TV.

580
23:26.440 --> 23:27.680
Went... went to the bathroom.

581
23:28.160 --> 23:29.079
That's... that's about it.

582
23:30.559 --> 23:31.440
Three days ago, didn't you

583
23:31.440 --> 23:32.480
get into a fight with Ma Guowen?

584
23:34.440 --> 23:35.480
Who... who said that?

585
23:35.599 --> 23:36.240
Who are you asking?

586
23:36.559 --> 23:37.440
I'm asking you.

587
23:37.839 --> 23:39.839
We know you had a clash with Ma Guowen.

588
23:39.839 --> 23:40.960
You went to see him three days ago.

589
23:41.440 --> 23:42.400
Did you two get physical?

590
23:42.559 --> 23:43.240
No, no, no.

591
23:43.359 --> 23:43.839
We didn't fight.

592
23:43.839 --> 23:45.160
We just... just argued a bit.

593
23:45.200 --> 23:46.319
No, no, no hands were thrown.

594
23:47.000 --> 23:47.599
After that,

595
23:47.799 --> 23:48.680
I never saw him again.

596
23:49.079 --> 23:50.079
What did you do the night before last?

597
23:52.000 --> 23:53.240
I... I don't know.

598
23:53.319 --> 23:53.920
The... the night before last...

599
23:54.000 --> 23:55.160
Weren't you watching TV at home?

600
23:55.319 --> 23:56.519
Eating, using the bathroom?

601
23:56.759 --> 23:57.279
That was...

602
23:57.359 --> 23:58.440
That was three... three nights ago.

603
23:58.640 --> 24:00.400
Didn't you go find Ma Guowen three nights ago?

604
24:03.839 --> 24:04.359
I...

605
24:04.720 --> 24:05.440
I... I... I...

606
24:05.920 --> 24:07.799
I... I can't really remember.

607
24:09.880 --> 24:10.279
Cao Jun.

608
24:10.279 --> 24:11.720
Playing dumb with me, are you?

609
24:12.200 --> 24:12.799
Let me tell you,

610
24:13.400 --> 24:14.839
we have all the time in the world to help you remember.

611
24:15.119 --> 24:15.960
Just sit there and think real hard.

612
24:43.559 --> 24:44.839
When did you start hauling cargo?

613
24:46.519 --> 24:47.200
Me?

614
24:47.599 --> 24:49.160
Started right after I left the factory.

615
24:49.599 --> 24:50.519
Kept at it ever since.

616
24:50.880 --> 24:52.000
We looked into it.

617
24:53.039 --> 24:54.880
Ever since Ma Guowen bought the factory,

618
24:55.119 --> 24:56.039
you've held a grudge against him.

619
24:56.759 --> 24:58.119
You went to help him move things,

620
24:58.720 --> 24:59.720
and smashed them up.

621
24:59.960 --> 25:00.359
Right?

622
25:00.720 --> 25:01.680
Ma Guowen chewed you out.

623
25:02.160 --> 25:02.920
Did that happen or not?

624
25:04.079 --> 25:05.680
I didn't break that stuff!

625
25:05.680 --> 25:06.240
Th-That...

626
25:06.519 --> 25:08.079
Ma Guowen framed me, he did!

627
25:08.240 --> 25:09.799
I don't care if he framed you

628
25:10.240 --> 25:11.359
or if you smashed it.

629
25:11.559 --> 25:12.319
It happened, didn't it?

630
25:13.839 --> 25:14.640
Cao Jun.

631
25:14.960 --> 25:16.400
I've jogged your memory enough.

632
25:16.519 --> 25:17.599
I'll ask you one more time.

633
25:19.720 --> 25:21.319
What were you doing the night before last?

634
25:23.880 --> 25:24.519
I...

635
25:26.480 --> 25:27.680
The night before last, I...

636
25:29.200 --> 25:29.680
The night before last...

637
25:30.000 --> 25:30.400
Right, right.

638
25:30.400 --> 25:31.559
I wasn't at home.

639
25:31.599 --> 25:32.599
Didn't... didn't go to the restroom.

640
25:32.599 --> 25:34.079
And I didn't go see Ma Guowen either.

641
25:34.079 --> 25:34.400
I...

642
25:34.920 --> 25:35.599
I, I, I...

643
25:35.960 --> 25:36.759
I was picking up fares.

644
25:37.599 --> 25:38.640
I was picking up fares on Guangyuan Road.

645
25:38.640 --> 25:39.400
I remember now.

646
25:39.839 --> 25:41.160
Right, lots of restaurants there,

647
25:41.200 --> 25:42.200
so there were plenty of passengers.

648
25:42.240 --> 25:44.119
I converted my little tricycle into a tuk-tuk!

649
25:44.200 --> 25:45.880
I was picking up fares on Guangyuan Road that night!

650
25:46.000 --> 25:46.400
Right, right, right.

651
25:46.400 --> 25:47.160
Ju-Just picking up fares.

652
25:47.240 --> 25:47.839
Are you sure?

653
25:47.880 --> 25:48.519
S-Sure! Absolutely sure.

654
25:48.519 --> 25:48.960
Picking up fares.

655
25:48.960 --> 25:49.759
Picking up fares on Guangyuan Road.

656
25:49.960 --> 25:51.240
Can anyone vouch for that?

657
25:59.240 --> 26:00.480
Look, Officer...

658
26:00.519 --> 26:02.279
You keep circling back to that night.

659
26:02.759 --> 26:03.920
Aren't you just trying to...

660
26:04.160 --> 26:04.799
You think that I...

661
26:04.880 --> 26:06.160
that I killed Ma Guowen?

662
26:06.240 --> 26:07.440
I didn't kill him!

663
26:07.599 --> 26:08.119
I wanted to, sure,

664
26:08.119 --> 26:09.880
but I didn't have the guts to kill Ma Guowen!

665
26:09.920 --> 26:11.000
Who said you killed Ma Guowen?

666
26:11.119 --> 26:11.960
Did I say that?

667
26:12.599 --> 26:13.799
You just blurted it out yourself.

668
26:22.680 --> 26:23.680
Let me ask you something.

669
26:24.039 --> 26:24.960
Do you know Shen Leshui well?

670
26:28.599 --> 26:29.839
You must be Li Mingyang.

671
26:30.359 --> 26:31.200
I'm Shen Leshui.

672
26:31.480 --> 26:31.880
Xiaoqin's friend.

673
26:31.880 --> 26:32.359
Here's some water.

674
26:35.000 --> 26:35.519
So...

675
26:35.799 --> 26:37.079
Can I sit here, Ms. Shen?

676
26:38.880 --> 26:39.240
Have a seat.

677
26:43.359 --> 26:45.200
I really didn't expect to run into you here.

678
26:45.799 --> 26:47.200
You've always been an idol of mine.

679
26:47.799 --> 26:48.680
Joining the TV station...

680
26:48.680 --> 26:49.960
I was just following in your footsteps.

681
26:50.400 --> 26:51.200
You're exaggerating.

682
26:51.319 --> 26:52.200
I'm nobody special.

683
26:52.440 --> 26:53.240
You're too modest.

684
26:53.759 --> 26:54.640
Lately,

685
26:54.720 --> 26:56.200
I've been covering social issues.

686
26:56.400 --> 26:58.359
I know you used to cover them too.

687
26:59.839 --> 27:01.680
Social issues are tough to report on.

688
27:02.119 --> 27:03.000
They really are.

689
27:05.359 --> 27:06.839
Reporting on social issues...

690
27:06.839 --> 27:07.880
You need to stick to the facts,

691
27:07.880 --> 27:09.160
be sharp and insightful,

692
27:09.200 --> 27:10.200
reveal life as it truly is,

693
27:10.519 --> 27:11.599
and have conviction,

694
27:11.599 --> 27:12.599
warmth, and passion.

695
27:12.799 --> 27:14.880
If you can't balance all three,

696
27:14.960 --> 27:16.200
it'll all crash and burn.

697
27:16.839 --> 27:17.680
"Crash and burn."

698
27:19.559 --> 27:20.960
That's quite a funny way to put it.

699
27:21.759 --> 27:23.359
I'm crashing and burning right now.

700
27:23.720 --> 27:24.559
You've got to be kidding.

701
27:24.599 --> 27:25.559
If you're going down,

702
27:25.559 --> 27:27.400
rookies like us wouldn't stand a chance.

703
27:28.000 --> 27:28.799
Are you a local?

704
27:29.240 --> 27:29.799
No.

705
27:30.000 --> 27:30.839
I'm from Qingzhou.

706
27:31.160 --> 27:32.119
Qingzhou, huh?

707
27:32.440 --> 27:33.359
How old are you?

708
27:33.480 --> 27:34.559
I'm 25 this year.

709
27:35.160 --> 27:35.799
What's wrong?

710
27:36.160 --> 27:37.880
I wanted to ask about someone.

711
27:38.000 --> 27:38.640
Who is it?

712
27:42.079 --> 27:43.160
Actually...

713
27:43.759 --> 27:45.079
I'm looking for someone.

714
27:45.240 --> 27:46.799
Tell you what, the person you're looking for...

715
27:46.799 --> 27:48.000
Just tell me their name.

716
27:50.640 --> 27:52.039
They're at your TV station.

717
27:52.680 --> 27:53.519
In our news department?

718
27:57.559 --> 27:58.480
As for him,

719
27:58.720 --> 27:59.519
he's not a bad guy.

720
28:00.079 --> 28:01.319
I just want to know

721
28:02.240 --> 28:03.559
who his parents are

722
28:03.559 --> 28:04.240
and where his home is.

723
28:05.559 --> 28:06.440
His home? His parents?

724
28:06.759 --> 28:08.559
You're helping a kid find their parents?

725
28:10.599 --> 28:11.039
Yes.

726
28:11.480 --> 28:12.880
That's a good thing, Sister Shen!

727
28:13.279 --> 28:14.319
Then just give me the child's

728
28:14.519 --> 28:15.559
name, gender, and age.

729
28:15.559 --> 28:16.359
Just tell me all that.

730
28:21.240 --> 28:22.000
I know, Sister Shen.

731
28:22.960 --> 28:24.039
This has to stay confidential.

732
28:24.279 --> 28:25.200
That's what matters most.

733
28:25.480 --> 28:25.880
Right?

734
28:26.039 --> 28:26.640
Don't worry.

735
28:26.880 --> 28:27.880
I won't let you down.

736
28:29.559 --> 28:30.000
All right.

737
28:31.240 --> 28:31.799
Shen Leshui,

738
28:32.640 --> 28:34.119
the female reporter who filmed

739
28:34.119 --> 28:35.039
that documentary back then...

740
28:38.960 --> 28:40.359
Yeah, there was someone like that.

741
28:40.799 --> 28:41.720
She interviewed me.

742
28:43.799 --> 28:45.559
When you workers gathered together

743
28:45.720 --> 28:46.680
to discuss buying the factory,

744
28:47.160 --> 28:48.519
all the way up to the auction,

745
28:48.880 --> 28:50.799
did she record the whole process on camera?

746
28:52.319 --> 28:52.839
She did.

747
28:53.680 --> 28:54.160
Whatever we said,

748
28:54.160 --> 28:55.160
she... she recorded it all.

749
29:05.079 --> 29:06.640
I've narrowed down our suspect pool:

750
29:07.400 --> 29:08.839
an able-bodied male

751
29:09.400 --> 29:11.440
connected to Ma Guowen or Lapi Brewery.

752
29:11.920 --> 29:12.599
Someone he knew,

753
29:13.079 --> 29:13.960
with a personal grudge.

754
29:14.559 --> 29:15.480
And what's more,

755
29:15.599 --> 29:16.880
has strong counter-investigation skills.

756
29:47.759 --> 29:48.160
Old Cao.

757
29:48.839 --> 29:49.400
You're here.

758
29:50.720 --> 29:51.400
Cold out there, huh?

759
30:24.519 --> 30:25.599
I won't— I'm not drinking his stuff.

760
30:26.160 --> 30:27.079
Don't be so eccentric.

761
30:38.839 --> 30:39.759
Everyone's here.

762
30:40.839 --> 30:41.359
You're here, Haipeng.

763
30:41.359 --> 30:41.880
Sit, sit, sit.

764
30:44.279 --> 30:45.000
What's up?

765
30:45.799 --> 30:46.720
Thought you weren't showing up?

766
30:46.720 --> 30:47.400
What?

767
30:47.559 --> 30:48.000
So what if I came out?

768
30:48.160 --> 30:49.079
What?

769
30:49.240 --> 30:50.079
Come on, Old Qian.

770
30:50.799 --> 30:52.400
Drinking here at Old Cheng's,

771
30:52.640 --> 30:53.480
and you brought your own booze?

772
30:56.160 --> 30:57.319
I just like this stuff, so what?

773
30:58.640 --> 31:00.039
Fine, he's just eccentric like that.

774
31:00.079 --> 31:00.720
Why even bother talking to him?

775
31:01.680 --> 31:02.559
He's busy these days,

776
31:03.240 --> 31:04.200
guarding the factory gate.

777
31:05.200 --> 31:08.079
Only him and Tieping are still factory workers.

778
31:09.000 --> 31:09.880
Tieping's got it good.

779
31:10.559 --> 31:11.680
He has an employment contract.

780
31:12.720 --> 31:14.039
I've always been a temp.

781
31:16.200 --> 31:17.559
Back in that old factory,

782
31:17.599 --> 31:18.440
there's just a pile of scrap.

783
31:18.480 --> 31:19.480
I just sit there watching it.

784
31:20.799 --> 31:21.519
Fair enough.

785
31:22.039 --> 31:22.720
Pretty fitting.

786
31:23.680 --> 31:24.599
Junk watching junk.

787
31:27.720 --> 31:29.079
Guess what that guy...

788
31:29.079 --> 31:30.160
what Ma Guowen told me a while back?

789
31:31.079 --> 31:31.759
Ma Guowen said,

790
31:32.160 --> 31:32.799
"Old Qian,

791
31:33.440 --> 31:34.880
you guarding the gate now,

792
31:34.960 --> 31:36.559
compared to when you were an accountant,

793
31:37.160 --> 31:38.799
contributes way more to our factory."

794
31:39.880 --> 31:40.960
I was like, "How so?"

795
31:42.680 --> 31:43.359
He said,

796
31:44.559 --> 31:46.319
"'Cause you've got a disability card now."

797
31:50.400 --> 31:51.279
That Ma Guowen,

798
31:51.599 --> 31:52.559
what a piece of shit.

799
31:53.759 --> 31:55.000
Serves him right getting killed.

800
31:57.680 --> 31:58.240
Haipeng,

801
31:59.400 --> 32:00.759
your ex-wife reported the crime.

802
32:03.839 --> 32:05.240
Making big moves right after she's back.

803
32:07.279 --> 32:08.079
Didn't they even

804
32:08.079 --> 32:09.279
haul me in for questioning?

805
32:10.240 --> 32:10.759
Cao Jun.

806
32:11.599 --> 32:11.960
Here.

807
32:13.759 --> 32:14.440
Calm your nerves.

808
32:19.680 --> 32:21.640
Who killed Ma Guowen anyway?

809
32:25.559 --> 32:26.599
Do you even need to guess?

810
32:32.920 --> 32:33.720
You did, obviously.

811
32:49.680 --> 32:50.079
Come on.

812
32:50.119 --> 32:51.200
Let's toast Old Qian.

813
32:51.279 --> 32:52.079
Cheers, cheers!

814
32:53.680 --> 32:54.160
Come on, Ping.

815
33:00.720 --> 33:01.359
Don't laugh.

816
33:01.400 --> 33:02.160
What are you laughing at?

817
33:02.759 --> 33:03.039
No, really.

818
33:03.720 --> 33:04.519
Old Qian, come on, over here.

819
33:04.559 --> 33:05.119
Tell us, tell us.

820
33:05.920 --> 33:07.160
Walk us through the crime.

821
33:07.960 --> 33:08.599
How'd you kill 'em?

822
33:28.519 --> 33:29.079
Who killed him?

823
33:46.480 --> 33:48.240
I dream of being the one.

824
33:49.240 --> 33:50.559
If the case ever gets solved,

825
33:50.599 --> 33:51.440
and I catch that punk,

826
33:51.440 --> 33:52.640
I'll slap him twice first.

827
33:53.759 --> 33:55.000
He stole my gig!

828
33:56.720 --> 33:58.000
Tell me, didn't Ma Guowen have it coming?

829
34:00.000 --> 34:00.880
Let's not go too far,

830
34:05.000 --> 34:05.839
look at Cao Jun.

831
34:07.880 --> 34:09.239
He won Model Worker several times, right?

832
34:09.320 --> 34:10.039
Just twice.

833
34:10.159 --> 34:11.239
Right, twice.

834
34:11.960 --> 34:12.880
I remember it clear as day.

835
34:13.559 --> 34:14.679
I handed you the bonus myself.

836
34:16.159 --> 34:17.320
Look at him now.

837
34:18.519 --> 34:19.679
If it weren't for Ma Guowen,

838
34:20.119 --> 34:20.960
and that...

839
34:22.039 --> 34:23.440
that tramp Liu Xuemei,

840
34:23.679 --> 34:24.920
would things ever come to this?

841
34:24.920 --> 34:25.559
Come on, stop.

842
34:25.800 --> 34:26.480
We were talking about Ma Guowen.

843
34:26.480 --> 34:27.480
Why drag Liu Xuemei into this?

844
34:27.599 --> 34:28.599
Why do you keep bringing her up?

845
34:28.639 --> 34:29.400
Yeah, why bring her up?

846
34:29.400 --> 34:30.039
If you want to say something,

847
34:30.039 --> 34:31.280
just say it already!

848
34:31.480 --> 34:32.000
Alright, alright.

849
34:32.000 --> 34:32.360
What?

850
34:32.360 --> 34:33.800
Driving a forklift or a tuk-tuk...

851
34:34.079 --> 34:34.880
Just drop it.

852
34:34.880 --> 34:35.559
You've had enough.

853
34:35.840 --> 34:37.280
He drinks all day long.

854
34:37.320 --> 34:38.559
Drinks liquor like water.

855
34:39.039 --> 34:39.480
Total drunkard.

856
34:39.480 --> 34:40.480
Just ignore him.

857
34:50.599 --> 34:51.360
Either way,

858
34:51.360 --> 34:52.039
let me make my stance clear.

859
34:52.920 --> 34:54.800
No matter who killed Ma Guowen,

860
34:57.199 --> 34:58.199
he's like a father to me.

861
35:07.639 --> 35:08.239
Go ahead.

862
35:15.199 --> 35:16.199
The reason I asked Cao Jun that

863
35:16.199 --> 35:16.639
was just

864
35:16.760 --> 35:18.320
to find out what happened back then.

865
35:23.760 --> 35:25.000
Right now,

866
35:25.280 --> 35:27.119
I'm really intrigued by this seven-year-old kid.

867
35:30.599 --> 35:31.519
Bro, I'm just wondering,

868
35:31.519 --> 35:32.400
does this kid

869
35:32.800 --> 35:34.480
really have anything to do with Ma Guowen's case?

870
35:35.039 --> 35:36.519
That was all information

871
35:37.159 --> 35:38.039
I just supplemented later.

872
35:39.599 --> 35:40.320
When we work a case,

873
35:40.320 --> 35:41.840
aren't we supposed to piece together

874
35:41.840 --> 35:42.679
all the information?

875
35:42.719 --> 35:43.599
As they say,

876
35:44.000 --> 35:44.960
follow every single trace,

877
35:45.440 --> 35:45.960
and pan for gold in the sand.

878
35:45.960 --> 35:46.519
Alright, alright, alright.

879
35:52.199 --> 35:53.119
Having an imagination

880
35:53.800 --> 35:54.360
is a good thing,

881
35:55.920 --> 35:56.760
but you can't just dream things up,

882
35:57.199 --> 35:58.039
and you can't make stuff up.

883
36:01.519 --> 36:02.079
Another thing,

884
36:02.599 --> 36:03.519
watch your attitude

885
36:04.239 --> 36:06.719
when you question witnesses.

886
36:09.559 --> 36:10.679
You know what I'm talking about, right?

887
36:10.840 --> 36:11.480
Got it.

888
36:12.760 --> 36:13.719
You can't jump to conclusions.

889
36:19.199 --> 36:20.159
"Got relatives in Lacheng?"

890
36:21.880 --> 36:22.920
"Haven't got a girlfriend or something?"

891
36:27.239 --> 36:28.320
The dead don't speak.

892
36:30.719 --> 36:31.960
I'm not talking about you.

893
36:32.679 --> 36:33.920
I mean the dead don't speak,

894
36:33.920 --> 36:35.880
and criminals won't just talk to us.

895
36:36.440 --> 36:38.400
So on a case, you've got to be patient and meticulous.

896
36:38.519 --> 36:41.199
Pan for gold from every trace of evidence.

897
36:41.639 --> 36:42.000
Right.

898
36:44.800 --> 36:45.920
"Right," my ass.

899
36:46.880 --> 36:48.159
You just said that earlier, didn't you?

900
36:48.400 --> 36:49.559
Those weren't my words.

901
36:49.599 --> 36:51.400
Brother Qiang used to say that to me all the time.

902
36:53.119 --> 36:53.519
Fine.

903
36:53.800 --> 36:54.599
Your Brother Qiang.

904
36:55.119 --> 36:55.760
Your Brother Qiang.

905
36:56.639 --> 36:57.519
Brother Chuang.

906
36:58.880 --> 37:00.400
Brother Qiang even told me to say hello to you.

907
37:01.639 --> 37:02.840
Say hello to me?

908
37:03.440 --> 37:04.719
I'd be lucky if he weren't badmouthing me.

909
37:06.000 --> 37:07.280
He won a Class-Three Merit.

910
37:07.880 --> 37:08.800
I'm a nobody.

911
37:11.280 --> 37:12.400
You won a Class-Three Merit too, right?

912
37:13.760 --> 37:15.000
I was just riding his coattails.

913
37:15.400 --> 37:17.599
It was a unit citation with Brother Qiang.

914
37:17.920 --> 37:20.000
A unit citation is still a Class-Three Merit.

915
37:21.840 --> 37:22.639
Well, that's just great.

916
37:23.400 --> 37:25.320
You could win a Class-Three Merit with Brother Qiang,

917
37:25.760 --> 37:27.440
but you won't get squat with me.

918
37:28.159 --> 37:28.719
What a pity.

919
37:32.039 --> 37:33.920
Bro, stop giving me grief, will you?

920
37:41.880 --> 37:42.280
Done eating?

921
37:42.960 --> 37:43.320
Done.

922
37:44.320 --> 37:44.760
Listen,

923
37:45.679 --> 37:46.960
go and warm up

924
37:47.199 --> 37:47.719
the car.

925
37:48.519 --> 37:49.320
I'll be right out after a phone call.

926
37:50.519 --> 37:51.159
Check, please!

927
37:51.199 --> 37:51.800
No, don't.

928
37:52.400 --> 37:52.960
I've got this.

929
37:54.199 --> 37:55.800
My treat for our Class-Three Merit hero.

930
37:57.440 --> 37:57.840
Thanks.

931
37:57.840 --> 37:58.519
Thanks, Brother Chuang.

932
38:49.280 --> 38:49.719
Come on.

933
38:50.159 --> 38:50.559
No, no, no.

934
38:51.079 --> 38:51.559
That's not it.

935
38:51.920 --> 38:52.480
Yan'er, Yan'er.

936
38:52.679 --> 38:53.440
Well... look, I...

937
38:53.880 --> 38:54.639
I asked you over...

938
38:54.679 --> 38:55.920
not because I wanted to...

939
38:56.280 --> 38:57.119
do... you know, that.

940
38:57.159 --> 38:59.199
I... I just wanted to chat.

941
38:59.320 --> 39:00.440
Have a heart-to-heart.

942
39:04.119 --> 39:05.119
Just have a chat.

943
39:07.280 --> 39:08.400
Then come on inside.

944
39:08.599 --> 39:09.400
Sit down and chat.

945
39:09.400 --> 39:10.159
Are we gonna talk standing up?

946
39:10.760 --> 39:11.440
Come on.

947
39:34.480 --> 39:35.239
We've been

948
39:35.559 --> 39:36.480
neighbors for years,

949
39:37.639 --> 39:38.719
and old coworkers too.

950
39:39.239 --> 39:40.239
Just chatting like this,

951
39:41.239 --> 39:42.199
why give me money?

952
39:43.880 --> 39:45.920
Doesn't this take up your time?

953
39:46.360 --> 39:47.800
Time is money,

954
39:47.960 --> 39:48.519
right?

955
39:51.480 --> 39:53.239
Time is all I've got these days.

956
39:56.199 --> 39:56.800
Let's chat.

957
39:57.719 --> 39:58.719
What do you want to talk about?

958
40:01.719 --> 40:02.719
What's the matter?

959
40:03.639 --> 40:04.960
Sighing and groaning like that.

960
40:06.639 --> 40:07.679
Who picked on you?

961
40:12.920 --> 40:14.079
I didn't kill Ma Guowen.

962
40:17.119 --> 40:18.320
Of course you didn't kill him.

963
40:19.000 --> 40:19.880
But they don't believe me.

964
40:20.480 --> 40:21.280
I believe you.

965
40:23.119 --> 40:24.159
I really wanted to kill him.

966
40:25.239 --> 40:26.159
But you didn't.

967
40:31.679 --> 40:32.920
Ma Guowen was an asshole.

968
40:34.000 --> 40:35.360
He bullied the weak and feared the strong.

969
40:36.079 --> 40:37.280
Always targeted easy marks.

970
40:38.840 --> 40:40.599
Back then, I just feared getting laid off.

971
40:41.079 --> 40:42.519
I didn't even dare claim my refund.

972
40:43.159 --> 40:44.320
Even then, he wouldn't let me off.

973
40:44.320 --> 40:45.320
He still told me to get lost.

974
40:46.440 --> 40:47.000
All right.

975
40:47.159 --> 40:48.239
Turn the page. It's in the past.

976
40:55.000 --> 40:56.039
I don't know what it is.

977
40:58.000 --> 40:59.159
Even though Ma Guowen is dead,

978
41:00.679 --> 41:01.760
I still can't feel happy.

979
41:11.599 --> 41:12.800
Ma Guowen

980
41:14.199 --> 41:16.239
was rotten to the core.

981
41:17.599 --> 41:18.719
He deserved to die anyway.

982
41:20.679 --> 41:23.239
If I'd known the police would treat me like a killer,

983
41:24.119 --> 41:25.039
I might as well have just...

984
41:25.119 --> 41:25.679
killed...

985
41:26.679 --> 41:27.119
Yeah.

986
41:28.039 --> 41:28.840
Over ten years ago,

987
41:28.880 --> 41:29.800
I already wanted to kill him.

988
41:35.239 --> 41:36.000
All right, that's enough.

989
41:38.440 --> 41:39.639
Don't let it eat away at you.

990
41:40.559 --> 41:41.400
The police

991
41:41.679 --> 41:42.280
are investigating,

992
41:42.360 --> 41:42.840
right?

993
41:43.199 --> 41:44.800
Of course they'll question people.

994
41:45.719 --> 41:47.079
You're not the only one they brought in.

995
41:48.039 --> 41:49.480
Old Qian was questioned too.

996
41:56.000 --> 41:56.840
How about this?

997
41:58.840 --> 42:00.599
Tomorrow I'll grab Cheng Youtian,

998
42:00.639 --> 42:01.800
Haipeng, and Tieping.

999
42:02.159 --> 42:03.480
We'll hold up big signs

1000
42:03.480 --> 42:04.599
right outside the police station and shout:

1001
42:05.320 --> 42:06.719
"Cao Jun is a good man!"

1002
42:06.840 --> 42:08.239
"Cao Jun didn't kill anyone!"

1003
42:08.320 --> 42:09.239
"Cao Jun is innocent!"

1004
42:09.239 --> 42:10.199
Shh, keep it down.

1005
42:10.400 --> 42:10.760
Don't shout.

1006
42:10.800 --> 42:12.039
Why are you yelling in the middle of the night?

1007
42:12.280 --> 42:13.119
Everyone can hear.

1008
42:13.639 --> 42:14.440
It looks bad.

1009
42:23.599 --> 42:24.079
Wait,

1010
42:24.599 --> 42:27.039
don't really go holding signs tomorrow.

1011
42:27.280 --> 42:28.920
Are you... really going to hold signs and shout?

1012
42:30.559 --> 42:31.400
You can't go!

1013
42:32.320 --> 42:33.199
Do you think I'm stupid?

1014
42:33.199 --> 42:34.039
Like I'd really go?

1015
42:34.440 --> 42:35.679
I'm not clueless like you.

1016
42:37.199 --> 42:37.679
Right.

1017
42:37.800 --> 42:39.239
I knew you wouldn't go.

1018
42:44.000 --> 42:45.199
Can you sleep now?

1019
42:47.639 --> 42:48.440
Then let's sleep.

1020
42:52.719 --> 42:53.480
How am I supposed to sleep?

1021
42:54.599 --> 42:55.559
Lie down and sleep!

1022
44:16.440 --> 44:17.400
At 7:30 this morning,

1023
44:17.400 --> 44:18.920
a worker from Lapi Brewery reported it.

1024
44:19.039 --> 44:20.559
He said this tuk-tuk belongs to Cao Jun.

1025
44:20.760 --> 44:21.760
Preliminary examination shows

1026
44:21.760 --> 44:23.440
the victim died of asphyxiation.

1027
44:23.800 --> 44:25.360
Whoever killed Cao Jun...

1028
44:26.119 --> 44:27.360
will die a horrible death.

1029
44:27.559 --> 44:29.000
Anyone who wanted to kill Cao Jun

1030
44:29.880 --> 44:31.239
definitely wouldn't kill Ma Guowen.

1031
44:32.360 --> 44:33.599
Who are you really?

1032
44:35.199 --> 44:37.039
What's your connection to Liu Xuemei?
